From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 12:22:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 69/69] web-app: clamp long message text with CSS, add show
 more/less toggle

Core no longer truncates long message text when writing to the database, so
the full text now reaches the UI. Clamp it visually instead: CSS
-webkit-line-clamp on the message body, with a "Show more"/"Show less"
button that only appears when the text is actually long (ported from core's
former truncation thresholds: >3800 chars or >38 lines). Text is never cut
in JS, so copy/select, in-page search and link parsing stay intact.

The existing hasHtml "Show Full Message" button is untouched; it still
covers real HTML mail and legacy truncated messages.

Show more/less labels go through tx() with new keys in
_locales/_untranslated_en.json, matching how every other fork-added label in
this codebase is done (export dialog, invite-link cards, message info,
sidebar resize) rather than hardcoding JSX string literals.
